*.log
# Server state. Guest profiles land in `data/<shard>/<id>.json`, one level deeper than the old
# `data/*.json` pattern reached — so running the server locally (which every capture script does)
# left real account files untracked and one careless `git add -A` away from the repository.
data/**/*.json
!data/.gitkeep

# `packages/client/public/models/` holds output from two different pipelines that write to the
# same directory, and only one of them can be committed.
#
#   ours    — `tools/blender/{build,props,portal}.py` generate every animal and every prop from
#             `animals.json` and `assets/meshy/`, both tracked. Deterministic output of tracked
#             sources, and ours to redistribute.
#   theirs  — `npm run assets:fetch` installs from `assets/packs.json`. Five of its six packs are
#             `source: manual`: Quaternius and Kenney are click-through downloads, so a build
#             machine cannot fetch them and they are not ours to put in the repo either.
#
# This used to ignore the whole directory, which kept *both* out — so a fresh checkout had no art
# at all. CI has none, the Docker image is built from a checkout so it has none, and the live
# deployment served procedural boxes while a local `docker build` shipped the real thing, because
# Docker reads this file's sibling rather than this file. Measured: /models/kangaroo.glb 404 in
# production.
#
# So: ours are tracked, and only the names that nothing but a pack can produce stay ignored. The
# animals a pack would install collide with ours by filename and cannot be separated here —
# installing those packs overwrites tracked files, and `git status` saying so is the point.
#
# `bear.glb` and `deer.glb` were on this list and have come off it. They were ignored as pack-only
# names, which was true while bear and deer were roadmap data; both are shipped animals now,
# generated by our own pipeline from `animals.json`. Leaving them ignored would have kept exactly
# two of the sixteen animals out of CI and out of the Docker image — the same "shipped with no
# art" failure this comment is about, at one ninth the size and correspondingly harder to notice.
# Caught by `animal-geometry.test.ts`, which reads every model an animal claims and would have
# gone red in CI while passing on the machine that generated them.
packages/client/public/models/fox-quaternius.glb
packages/client/public/models/anim/
packages/client/public/models/audio/
packages/client/public/models/props/bush.glb
packages/client/public/models/props/grass.glb
packages/client/public/models/props/rock.glb
packages/client/public/models/props/rock-kenney.glb
packages/client/public/models/props/tree.glb
packages/client/public/models/props/tree-kenney.glb

# Store packaging. There are two Android targets now — packaging/meta-quest (Horizon Store) and
# packaging/android-phone (Google Play) — and they generate byte-for-byte the same *kinds* of
# files, so these patterns are written against `packaging/*/` rather than named per target. A
# third target must not be able to leak a keystore by virtue of nobody remembering this file.
#
# twa-manifest.json is rendered per-environment by `npm run pack:quest` / `pack:phone` (it embeds
# one origin), and the signing key must never be committed: a store binds a listing to that key
# forever, so leaking it hands over the ability to publish updates as us.
packaging/*/twa-manifest.json
packaging/**/*.keystore
packaging/**/*.jks
packaging/**/*.apk
packaging/**/*.apk.idsig
packaging/**/*.aab
packaging/**/assetlinks.json

# The Android projects under packaging/ are generated by `bubblewrap update` from twa-manifest.json
# on every build. Committing them would mean reviewing a regenerated Gradle project on each domain
# change, and they would go stale the moment the manifest did.
packaging/*/app/
packaging/*/gradle/
packaging/*/gradlew
packaging/*/gradlew.bat
packaging/*/build.gradle
packaging/*/settings.gradle
packaging/*/gradle.properties
packaging/*/store_icon.png
packaging/*/manifest-checksum.txt
packaging/*/.gradle/
packaging/*/build/

# The Microsoft Store package. AppxManifest.xml carries the Partner Center identity, which is
# per-account and must not be committed; the tile art is regenerated from icons/icon-1024.png by
# `npm run pack:msstore`, so committing it would only let it drift from the source icon.
packaging/microsoft-store/build/
packaging/*/listing/
packaging/**/*.msix
packaging/**/*.msixbundle
packaging/**/*.appx
packaging/**/*.appxbundle
packaging/**/*.pfx

# Blender generator: bytecode, and the spec it reads. The spec is dumped from the game data by
# `npm run assets:spec`, so a committed copy could only ever be a stale second source of truth.
__pycache__/
tools/blender/animals.json

# Agent worktrees are separate checkouts of this repository. `git add -A` from the root picked
# two of them up as embedded-repository gitlinks once; they must never enter the index.
.claude/worktrees/
